  "articleBody": "Ever walk into your bedroom and feel like the lighting just isn't working? You're not alone! A lot of common mistakes can make your bedroom lighting feel off, but thankfully, they're often fixable. One major blunder is relying solely on a single, bright ceiling fixture. This creates harsh, uninviting light and doesn't allow for flexibility. You need layers of light! Another frequent issue is choosing bulbs that are too harsh or have the wrong color temperature for nighttime use. Warm white bulbs are usually best for a relaxing bedroom. Ignoring the need for dimming is also a big one; dimmers let you control the mood and brightness, which is crucial in a bedroom. Don't forget to account for fixture height, glare, and switch access either. No one wants to get out of bed to turn off the light! If you're struggling with these issues, think about what you want your lighting to accomplish: relaxation, reading, getting dressed? Then, consider ambient, task, and accent lighting. For more complex projects involving new wiring or circuit changes, it's wise to bring in a professional electrician. They can help ensure everything is up to code and perfectly suited to your needs.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
